## 14. Validation plan

**Executed by candidate (W, in admitted isolation; receipts in `witnesses.json`):**
- **[W-1]** source→project integer mapping: monotonicity, exact 1.000 s case, round-half-even tie behavior, and the downsampling collision (1000,1001 → 500) proving source-side anchoring. Scope: arithmetic check, no media/GUI.
- **[W-2]** gap-insertion drift: naive time-anchored cue resolves into inserted silence (`None`), content-anchored cue survives at 15.0 s. Scope: two-clip toy model.
- **[W-3]** crossfade gain tables: linear keeps amplitude-sum 1 (identical material unity), equal-power keeps power-sum 1 (−3 dB vs +3 dB cases). Scope: numeric gain tables only; no listening claims.
- **[W-4]** WAV chunk parse: fmt/data consistency on a generated file; truncated copy raises the declared-vs-observed ambiguity flag. Scope: stdlib parser demo, not the libsndfile-based media layer.

**Proposed / UNEXECUTED (V; required before any release):**
- **[V-1]** golden-content render: synthetic sources → trim/gap/join(transition) → export; assert exported samples equal an independently computed sample-exact concatenation including the transition region; assert resample output sample count matches `round_half_even` prediction.
- **[V-2]** save/close/relocate/reopen: all cue anchors bit-identical after digest-based media resolution; orphan flags only where trims removed anchors.
- **[V-3]** cancel render mid-write → manifest state `cancelled`, artifact named `*.cancelled`, export list shows no `complete`.
- **[V-4]** 2 h synthetic import + render on 8 GB-class hardware: RSS < 350 MiB, index < 60 s, cancel latency < 1 s, render ≥ 2× realtime. (Gate for Alt A trigger, §6.)
- **[V-5]** > 4 GiB export produces RF64; import of a clamped-header (and a wrapped-header) WAV raises the §5 flag. (Wrapped-header sample generation pending L3 evidence.)
- **[V-6]** contradiction handling: truncated/contradictory media blocks export until acknowledged (extends W4 to the app).
- **[V-7]** two-editor exchange drill: folder copied, media moved, one editor resolves by digest, `edit_log` conveys prior edits; no original file mtime/bytes changed (checksum audit).
- **[V-8]** keyboard-only walkthrough + screen-reader label audit on one OS.
- **[V-9]** startup dependency assertion: libsndfile runtime version ≥ 1.2.1 else refuse large-file writes.

## 15. Limits of this research (not established here)

- No application, GUI, or libsndfile call was executed in this stage; W1–W4 are isolated component checks. All architectural performance numbers are proposals gated by V4.
- The #930 chain establishes the write-side fix and its release; read-side behavior, RF64 semantics of the all-ones size field (L2), and existence/absence of any later test coverage beyond commit-search evidence (L3) remain open.
- Tier-2 decode determinism (L8), ELAN EAF details (L1), transcription/noise-reduction opportunities (L5, L6) are leads, not findings.
- Two requested catalog URLs 404'd during discovery (Sonic Visualiser reference manual path; MLT `main` branch header) and are recorded as negative evidence (S13, S14); the substitute sources used are pinned.

